{
  "dom_id": "step-e271",
  "name": "Example: Interpreting the Derivative of a Function in a Given Context",
  "problem": "The function $B(s)$ models a school's budget, in dollars, given the average number of students $s$ in each grade. What is the best interpretation of $B'(30)=2\\,000?$",
  "worked_solution": "The function $B'(s)$ represents the rate at which the budget is changing at the moment when the school has an average of exactly $s$ students in each grade.\n\nTherefore, $B'(30) = 2\\,000$ means:\n\n*When the school has an average of $30$ students in each grade, its budget is increasing at a rate of $2\\,000$ dollars per student.*",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
